e"}],"gloss":"fame"},{"surface":"பேகன்","parts":[{"text":"பேகன்","lemma":"pēkaṉ","gloss":"Pegan"}],"gloss":"Pegan"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஒல்லென","parts":[{"text":"ஒல்லென","lemma":"olleṉa","gloss":"with the sound 'ol'"}],"gloss":"with the sound 'ol'"},{"surface":"ஒலிக்கும்","parts":[{"text":"ஒலிக்கும்","lemma":"olikkum","gloss":"resounding"}],"gloss":"resounding"},{"surface":"தேரொடு","parts":[{"text":"தேரொடு","lemma":"tēroṭu","gloss":"with the chariot"}],"gloss":"with the chariot"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"முல்லை","parts":[{"text":"முல்லை","lemma":"mullai","gloss":"jasmine"}],"gloss":"jasmine"},{"surface":"வேலி","parts":[{"text":"வேலி","lemma":"veli","gloss":"fence"}],"gloss":"fence"},{"surface":"நல்","parts":[{"text":"நல்","lemma":"nal","gloss":"good"}],"gloss":"good"},{"surface":"ஊரானே","parts":[{"text":"ஊரானே","lemma":"ūrāṉē","gloss":"he of the town"}],"gloss":"he of the town"}]}],"literal":"Your not showing grace is indeed cruel! As darkness comes, / tuning the small lute to the cevvaḻi melody, O friend, your / forest that welcomes the rainy season, as we sang, / like the blue fragrant water-lily, her collyrium-painted eyes / dimmed with tears, flowing with streaks of tears, drenching her chest adorned with ornaments, / as she did not cease to grieve, \"O young woman! / You are indeed a relative to our friend who desires you,\" saying, / as we bowed and asked her, wiping with her fingers / that resemble the buds of the flame lily, her tears, / \"We are not his relatives, listen now! / Desiring the beauty of a woman like me, always / he will come, they say, Pegan of shining fame, / with his chariot that resounds with the sound 'ol', / in the good town with jasmine fences.\"","translation":"Your refusal to show grace is truly cruel! As darkness fell, we tuned our small lute to the cevvaḻi melody and sang of your forest that welcomes the rainy season. Then, a young woman, whose collyrium-painted eyes—once beautiful like the fragrant blue water-lily—were dimmed with tears that flowed in streaks and drenched her jeweled chest, wept without ceasing. We bowed to her and asked, 'O young woman, are you a relative of our beloved friend?' Wiping her tears with fingers that resembled the buds of the flame lily, she replied, 'We are not his relatives. Listen! Desiring the beauty of some other woman like me, Pegan of illustrious fame will always go with his loud-sounding chariot to that good town fenced with jasmine.'","modern":"உன்னுடைய அருள் செய்யாமை மிகவும் கொடியது! இருள் வரும் வேளையில், சிறிய யாழில் செவ்வழிப் பண்ணை இசைத்து, உன்னுடைய கார் காலத்தை வரவேற்கும் காட்டைப் பற்றி நாங்கள் பாடினோம். அப்போது, நீல நிற நறுமணமுள்ள நெய்தல் மலரைப் போன்ற மை தீட்டிய கண்கள் அழுது, பெருகிய கண்ணீர்த் துளிகள் மார்பில் அணிந்த அணிகலன்களை நனைக்க, வருந்துவதை நிறுத்தாத ஒரு பெண்ணைக் கண்டோம். 'இளம்பெண்ணே! எங்களை விரும்பும் எங்கள் நண்பனாகிய பேகனுக்கு நீ உறவினளா?' என்று நாங்கள் அவளை வணங்கி வினவினோம். காந்தள் மொட்டுப் போன்ற தன் விரல்களால் கண்ணீரைத் துடைத்துக் கொண்டு அவள் கூறினாள்: 'நாங்கள் அவனுடைய உறவினர் அல்லேம், இப்போது கேள்! என்னைப்போன்ற வேறொரு பெண்ணின் அழகை விரும்பி, விளங்கும் புகழையுடைய பேகன், ஒல்லென்று ஒலிக்கும் தன் தேருடன், முல்லை வேலியையுடைய நல்லூருக்கு எப்போதும் செல்வான் என்று கூறுவர்.'","explanation":"The poet Kapilar is addressing King Vaiyāvik Kōpperum Pēkaṉ, who has abandoned his wife, Kaṇṇaki, to live with a courtesan in another town. Kapilar describes how he and his fellow bards visited Pegan's forest at dusk, played the melancholic cevvaḻi melody on their small lute, and encountered a weeping woman. When they respectfully asked if she was related to their patron Pegan, she wiped her tears with fingers resembling flame-lily buds and bitterly denied any relationship. She told them that Pegan instead spends his time visiting another woman in Nallūr, a town fenced with jasmine. The contrast between her tear-dimmed eyes and the vibrant, jasmine-fenced town of Nallūr highlights her profound isolation and grief.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.56],[0.56,0.8],[0.8,1.5],[1.5,2.1],[2.1,2.9],[2.9,3.0],[3.0,3.5],[3.5,3.7],[3.7,4.1],[4.1,5.2],[5.2,5.6],[5.6,6.0],[6.0,6.1],[6.1,7.3],[7.3,7.5],[7.5,8.3],[8.3,8.3],[8.3,9.3],[9.3,9.3],[9.3,9.3],[9.3,9.3],[9.3,9.3],[9.3,9.3],[9.3,12.3],[12.3,12.6],[12.6,12.7],[12.7,13.5],[13.5,14.3],[14.3,14.4],[14.7,14.9],[14.9,15.3],[15.46,15.7],[15.7,16.0],[16.0,16.4],[16.4,17.1],[17.1,17.2],[17.2,17.6],[18.52,19.32],[19.32,19.72],[19.72,20.02],[20.23,21.08],[21.08,21.3],[21.3,21.3],[21.3,21.3],[21.3,22.92],[22.92,23.12],[23.17,23.22],[23.22,24.42],[24.42,24.52],[24.52,25.32],[25.32,25.82],[25.82,26.82],[26.82,27.22],[27.22,27.42],[27.42,28.02],[28.02,28.12],[28.12,28.92],[28.92,28.92],[28.92,29.82],[29.82,30.92],[30.92,31.22],[31.22,31.61],[31.61,31.84]],"female":[[0.0,0.57],[0.57,1.2],[1.2,1.7],[1.7,2.3],[2.3,2.9],[2.9,3.0],[3.0,3.5],[3.5,3.8],[3.8,4.3],[4.3,5.5],[5.5,6.0],[6.0,6.5],[6.5,6.6],[6.6,7.8],[7.8,8.2],[8.2,8.6],[8.6,8.9],[8.9,10.41],[10.41,10.41],[10.41,10.73],[10.73,10.73],[10.73,10.73],[10.73,12.3],[12.3,13.1],[13.1,13.5],[13.5,13.7],[13.7,14.7],[14.7,15.6],[15.6,15.9],[16.1,16.3],[16.3,16.97],[16.97,17.22],[17.3,17.6],[17.6,18.6],[18.6,19.2],[19.2,19.3],[19.3,19.7],[20.76,21.56],[21.56,22.16],[22.16,22.36],[22.36,22.7],[22.79,22.87],[22.96,24.36],[24.36,24.85],[25.34,25.46],[25.46,25.76],[25.76,26.16],[26.16,27.36],[27.36,27.36],[27.36,28.16],[28.16,28.86],[28.86,29.76],[29.76,30.26],[30.26,30.76],[30.76,31.36],[31.36,31.46],[31.46,32.56],[32.56,32.66],[32.66,33.66],[33.66,34.36],[34.36,35.06],[35.06,35.45],[35.45,35.68]]},"sync":[[["அருளாய்","you do not show grace"]],[["அருளாய்","you do not show grace"],["ஆகலோ","being so"]],[["கொடிதே","is indeed cruel"]],[["இருள்","darkness"],["வர","to come"]],[["சீறியாழ்","small lute"]],[["செவ்வழி","cevvaḻi melody"]],[["பண்ணி","having tuned"]],[["யாழ","O friend"]],[["நின்","your"]],[["கார்","rainy season"],["எதிர்","welcoming"]],[["கானம்","forest"]],[["பாடினேம்","we sang"]],[["பாடினேம்","we sang"],["ஆக","as"]],[["நீல்